{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014doEqrzcfoUG9uLrmJTubv","type":"tool_result","content":"total 5872\ndrwxr-xr-x 5 micha micha    4096 Nov  5 16:21 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 micha micha    4096 Nov  5 16:21 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  248164 Dec 31  1979 API.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   15883 Dec 31  1979 ASSETS.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   57520 Dec 31  1979 CHANGELOG.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   41812 Dec 31  1979 CREDITS.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   60159 Dec 31  1979 GUIDE.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  176448 Dec 31  1979 LIBRARY.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha    1071 Dec 31  1979 LICENSE\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha    3151 Dec 31  1979 README.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   30347 Dec 31  1979 check.mjs\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 micha micha    4096 Nov  5 16:21 examples\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha    4526 Dec 31  1979 game.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha     506 Dec 31  1979 index.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  431976 Dec 31  1979 library.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   18064 Dec 31  1979 manifest.json\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 micha micha    4096 Nov  5 16:21 packs\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha     226 Dec 31  1979 pixel-engine.d.ts\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 4864228 Dec 31  1979 pixel-engine.js\ndrwxr-xr-x 4 micha micha    4096 Nov  5 16:21 types\n248164 API.md\n 15883 ASSETS.md\n 57520 CHANGELOG.md\n 41812 CREDITS.md\n 60159 GUIDE.md\n176448 LIBRARY.md\n  3151 README.md\n603137 total\n# Changelog\n\nWhat changed in Pixel Engine for a game built on it, newest first. The version is\n`package.json`'s; a game reads it as `ENGINE_VERSION`, `Engine.version` or\n`engine.state().version`. The engine kit (`npm run bundle`, docs/GUIDE.md) ships this file.\n\nWhen a change alters the public API (`src/bundle.ts` exports) or something a game can see,\nbump the version (minor while it is 0.x) and add its section here; `npm test` fails when\n`package.json`'s version has no section.\n\n## 0.46.0\n\n- **No more handoff page**: the engine's site is gone, so `manifest.json` has no `handoff` and the\n  kit's `README.md` no longer names a page for agents. Newer kits are where they were:\n  `latest` (the newest release's zip), `releases` and `source`.\n\n## 0.45.0\n\n- **The kit runs in Node**: `Engine.headless(game, { assets })` from `pixel-engine.js` alone, with\n  no `node_modules`. In Node, Rapier's wasm comes from the data URL the kit inlines, and a reader\n  (`assets`, `setAssetReader`) no longer sees the files the kit embeds (`__PIXEL_ASSETS__`: the\n  built-in models load as they do in a page).\n- **`node check.mjs --headless game.js`**: plays a game module in Node, no browser. It makes the game\n  with the module's `createGame()` export, plays the `--keys` frames, replays the recording in a\n  fresh game and writes `report.json` (`state()`, errors, the fingerprint). Exit 1 on an error or a\n  replay that ends elsewhere, 2 for a page or a module without `createGame()`.\n- **The starter `game.js` exports `createGame()`** and starts the engine only where there is a\n  `document`, so it imports in Node. GUIDE.md section 8, *Play it in Node*, shows a test of your own.\n\n## 0.44.0","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b7f78278-523d-4db5-bad6-0b641e53d240","uuid":"a4abc507-2c6a-44d7-bae8-a1aadb70ee86","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:21:18.549Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"total 5872\ndrwxr-xr-x 5 micha micha    4096 Nov  5 16:21 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 micha micha    4096 Nov  5 16:21 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  248164 Dec 31  1979 API.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   15883 Dec 31  1979 ASSETS.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   57520 Dec 31  1979 CHANGELOG.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   41812 Dec 31  1979 CREDITS.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   60159 Dec 31  1979 GUIDE.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  176448 Dec 31  1979 LIBRARY.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha    1071 Dec 31  1979 LICENSE\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha    3151 Dec 31  1979 README.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   30347 Dec 31  1979 check.mjs\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 micha micha    4096 Nov  5 16:21 examples\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha    4526 Dec 31  1979 game.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha     506 Dec 31  1979 index.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  431976 Dec 31  1979 library.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   18064 Dec 31  1979 manifest.json\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 micha micha    4096 Nov  5 16:21 packs\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha     226 Dec 31  1979 pixel-engine.d.ts\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 4864228 Dec 31  1979 pixel-engine.js\ndrwxr-xr-x 4 micha micha    4096 Nov  5 16:21 types\n248164 API.md\n 15883 ASSETS.md\n 57520 CHANGELOG.md\n 41812 CREDITS.md\n 60159 GUIDE.md\n176448 LIBRARY.md\n  3151 README.md\n603137 total\n# Changelog\n\nWhat changed in Pixel Engine for a game built on it, newest first. The version is\n`package.json`'s; a game reads it as `ENGINE_VERSION`, `Engine.version` or\n`engine.state().version`. The engine kit (`npm run bundle`, docs/GUIDE.md) ships this file.\n\nWhen a change alters the public API (`src/bundle.ts` exports) or something a game can see,\nbump the version (minor while it is 0.x) and add its section here; `npm test` fails when\n`package.json`'s version has no section.\n\n## 0.46.0\n\n- **No more handoff page**: the engine's site is gone, so `manifest.json` has no `handoff` and the\n  kit's `README.md` no longer names a page for agents. Newer kits are where they were:\n  `latest` (the newest release's zip), `releases` and `source`.\n\n## 0.45.0\n\n- **The kit runs in Node**: `Engine.headless(game, { assets })` from `pixel-engine.js` alone, with\n  no `node_modules`. In Node, Rapier's wasm comes from the data URL the kit inlines, and a reader\n  (`assets`, `setAssetReader`) no longer sees the files the kit embeds (`__PIXEL_ASSETS__`: the\n  built-in models load as they do in a page).\n- **`node check.mjs --headless game.js`**: plays a game module in Node, no browser. It makes the game\n  with the module's `createGame()` export, plays the `--keys` frames, replays the recording in a\n  fresh game and writes `report.json` (`state()`, errors, the fingerprint). Exit 1 on an error or a\n  replay that ends elsewhere, 2 for a page or a module without `createGame()`.\n- **The starter `game.js` exports `createGame()`** and starts the engine only where there is a\n  `document`, so it imports in Node. GUIDE.md section 8, *Play it in Node*, shows a test of your own.\n\n## 0.44.0","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014doEqrzcfoUG9uLrmJTubv","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
