{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkunL53GVu6juPJ65SSS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HARWDexwyEYWmfDgPPVj9a","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162042__x14746a/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='exit-interview.json'\nj=json.load(open(p))\nj['sourceInformation']['research']=\"Read the plan, the kit guide, ASSETS.md and the hub README before building; no other research\"\nj['testingFeedback']=[\n \"34 issues were caught by scripts and tests and logged in tests/ISSUES.md: unreachable scripted spawns and drops, a quest step that advanced through a locked exit, a loot view crash, boss-arena walls that never lifted, monsters deadlocked at doorways, a class picker that always chose the last card, pause and hero screens that closed the frame they opened, a second pad's Options pausing the first player, 49 layout overflows, an XP compounding bug, and a hub session that never started its simulation.\",\n \"13 of them would have been critical or game breaking: the Bursar's coin crash, the missing arena exits, permanent boss walls, the missing relic interaction, lychgates inside walls, doorway deadlocks, the class picker, the pause menu that could not open, the pad pause conflict, scripted spawns inside walls, the tutorial full of monsters, the quest step skipping a locked exit, and the hub session that never stepped.\",\n \"The whole-game playthrough by a bot, played through the real menus by key presses. It found most of the softlocks and the logic errors that no unit test would have thought to ask about. The two-frame hub game test was next: it caught the session that never started even though the harness passed.\",\n \"The text lints (banned names, TODO words, HUD font characters) and screenshots of the title. The lints found only words in comments, and a title screenshot proves very little once the layout test exists.\"]\nj['engineFeedback']=[\n \"One module that holds everything: three.js, Rapier, the hero rig with 78 clips, the toon pixel renderer, audio synthesis and a headless mode. Stepping frames by hand with engine.step, recording and replaying with a matching fingerprint, and checking models with the sheets tool made a very large game testable in Node.\",\n \"Yes. NavGrid centres its grid on the origin unless you pass an origin, which made every path fail until I did. The pixel HUD is 427 by 240 art pixels on a 720p window but 480 by 270 headless, so layouts built for one overflowed in the other. Pads are merged into one input, so couch co-op needed my own pad reader.\",\n \"The whole simulation and its rules (skills as data ops, loot, monsters, zones from ASCII rooms, bosses, quests), an immediate-mode UI with focus movement for pad, mouse and keyboard, a per-seat input router, the hub netcode, the Animalese voices and the bot that plays the game.\",\n \"Getting a lot of authored content to read at 480 by 270: pixel text only, no wrapping helpers, and a HUD that is a canvas. Also running anything with many actors, ragdolls and lights under software WebGPU, which is slow enough that everything had to be checked by stepping frames rather than watching.\",\n \"none\",\n \"Expose the audio output so a test can read levels without wrapping AudioNode.prototype.connect, read each gamepad separately instead of merging them, and make the headless HUD the same size as a 720p page.\"]\nj['promptFeedback']=[\n \"The plan was detailed and mostly verified on this machine: the build order, the never-cut list, the netcode budgets, the test tiers and the exact flags to start the browser with saved a great deal of guessing.\",\n \"How much was expected in one run. Three classes with 24 skills and 72 Tones, three bosses, a hub session with its own card and netcode, four test tiers and a screen for everything is a large game for one sitting. The pacing target of about 60 minutes conflicts with a bot that clears every room, and the art size differs between the plan (480 by 270) and a real 720p window.\",\n \"Making the playthrough bot reliable. Most of the real bugs surfaced only when a script tried to finish the game by pathing through generated rooms with crowds, doorways and bosses, and every softlock cost a full replay.\",\n \"Cut the scope to something that fits, or give a reference bot with pathing and stuck handling, and say plainly which art size the HUD layout must target. State the XP target as a number of kills as well as a level, since a clear-everything bot and a human reach very different levels.\"]\njson.dump(j, open(p,'w'), indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\nprint(len(j['testingFeedback']), len(j['engineFeedback']), len(j['promptFeedback']))\nEOF\ncd TollBoothOfDoom-Diablo3-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261105-162042 && node tools/genabout.mjs; timeout 60 bash -c 'until grep -q \"^done\" tests/hub-run/dump.txt; do sleep 2; done'; grep -E \"MOVETEST|DUMPX\" tests/hub-run/dump.txt | cut -c1-300"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1334,"cache_read_input_tokens":788421,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1334},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b7f78278-523d-4db5-bad6-0b641e53d240","uuid":"1f6e4081-1042-47b2-b6bd-3d272b7f05d0","timestamp":"2026-11-06T02:47:53.739Z","request_id":"req_011CgkunKix46NvZA7g921Gr","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01HARWDexwyEYWmfDgPPVj9a":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162042__x14746a/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='exit-interview.json'\nj=json.load(open(p))\nj['sourceInformation']['research']=\"Read the plan, the kit guide, ASSETS.md and the hub README before building; no other research\"\nj['testingFeedback']=[\n \"34 issues were caught by scripts and tests and logged in tests/ISSUES.md: unreachable scripted spawns and drops, a quest step that advanced through a locked exit, a loot view crash, boss-arena walls that never lifted, monsters deadlocked at doorways, a class picker that always chose the last card, pause and hero screens that closed the frame they opened, a second pad's Options pausing the first player, 49 layout overflows, an XP compounding bug, and a hub session that never started its simulation.\",\n \"13 of them would have been critical or game breaking: the Bursar's coin crash, the missing arena exits, permanent boss walls, the missing relic interaction, lychgates inside walls, doorway deadlocks, the class picker, the pause menu that could not open, the pad pause conflict, scripted spawns inside walls, the tutorial full of monsters, the quest step skipping a locked exit, and the hub session that never stepped.\",\n \"The whole-game playthrough by a bot, played through the real menus by key presses. It found most of the softlocks and the logic errors that no unit test would have thought to ask about. The two-frame hub game test was next: it caught the session that never started even though the harness passed.\",\n \"The text lints (banned names, TODO words, HUD font characters) and screenshots of the title. The lints found only words in comments, and a title screenshot proves very little once the layout test exists.\"]\nj['engineFeedback']=[\n \"One module that holds everything: three.js, Rapier, the hero rig with 78 clips, the toon pixel renderer, audio synthesis and a headless mode. Stepping frames by hand with engine.step, recording and replaying with a matching fingerprint, and checking models with the sheets tool made a very large game testable in Node.\",\n \"Yes. NavGrid centres its grid on the origin unless you pass an origin, which made every path fail until I did. The pixel HUD is 427 by 240 art pixels on a 720p window but 480 by 270 headless, so layouts built for one overflowed in the other. Pads are merged into one input, so couch co-op needed my own pad reader.\",\n \"The whole simulation and its rules (skills as data ops, loot, monsters, zones from ASCII rooms, bosses, quests), an immediate-mode UI with focus movement for pad, mouse and keyboard, a per-seat input router, the hub netcode, the Animalese voices and the bot that plays the game.\",\n \"Getting a lot of authored content to read at 480 by 270: pixel text only, no wrapping helpers, and a HUD that is a canvas. Also running anything with many actors, ragdolls and lights under software WebGPU, which is slow enough that everything had to be checked by stepping frames rather than watching.\",\n \"none\",\n \"Expose the audio output so a test can read levels without wrapping AudioNode.prototype.connect, read each gamepad separately instead of merging them, and make the headless HUD the same size as a 720p page.\"]\nj['promptFeedback']=[\n \"The plan was detailed and mostly verified on this machine: the build order, the never-cut list, the netcode budgets, the test tiers and the exact flags to start the browser with saved a great deal of guessing.\",\n \"How much was expected in one run. Three classes with 24 skills and 72 Tones, three bosses, a hub session with its own card and netcode, four test tiers and a screen for everything is a large game for one sitting. The pacing target of about 60 minutes conflicts with a bot that clears every room, and the art size differs between the plan (480 by 270) and a real 720p window.\",\n \"Making the playthrough bot reliable. Most of the real bugs surfaced only when a script tried to finish the game by pathing through generated rooms with crowds, doorways and bosses, and every softlock cost a full replay.\",\n \"Cut the scope to something that fits, or give a reference bot with pathing and stuck handling, and say plainly which art size the HUD layout must target. State the XP target as a number of kills as well as a level, since a clear-everything bot and a human reach very different levels.\"]\njson.dump(j, open(p,'w'), indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\nprint(len(j['testingFeedback']), len(j['engineFeedback']), len(j['promptFeedback']))\nEOF\ncd TollBoothOfDoom-Diablo3-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261105-162042 && node tools/genabout.mjs; timeout 60 bash -c 'until grep -q \"^done\" tests/hub-run/dump.txt; do sleep 2; done'; grep -E \"MOVETEST|DUMPX\" tests/hub-run/dump.txt | cut -c1-300"}}}
