{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgm7DpCS1jurvGYg7oYia","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I did more of what PLAN.md asks, but four items are still open: Malison's arms are not driven, the Crawler's legs are only bounded, the 60-minute pace is unchecked, and a few listed screens went unseen.\n\nFinal test results on the last build:\n- **sim:** 1769 checks, 0 failures.\n- **browser:** 58 checks, 0 failures.\n- **hub:** 10 checks, 0 failures.\n- **shell, smoke, Last Bell and the Bellwarden playthrough:** 206 checks, 0 failures. I did not re-run the Lamplighter and Sexton playthroughs after these changes.\n\nWhat changed this turn:\n- **Boss entrances:** letterbox bars and a camera zoom on the boss, with the sim held for about 2.6 seconds. This is outside hub sessions.\n- **Opening and ending:** they are now camera cutscenes. The opening plays over St. Clement's Yard and the ending over the Belfry. The camera drifts and zooms under letterbox bars, with the narrator's line as a subtitle and the HUD hidden. They can be skipped.\n- **Leg animation:** the Tomb Crawler, Clapperjaw and Collection Plate now have jointed legs that swing as they move.\n- **Malison's arms:** her four arms are now separate jointed parts that sway and lash harder on attacks. They are not driven by the engine's spring or arm-solver tools, which the plan called for.\n- **Screens fixed:** the map footer no longer overlaps the prompts and its zone names are shorter. The HUD no longer shows behind dialogue. `exit-interview.json` and the About screen now describe the animation accurately.\n- **Screens looked at this turn:** the Pennywhistle vendor screen, map, dialogue, Knell Font setup, Cloister, Belfry, About, the opening cutscene, and the Bursar and Malison arenas. Together with the earlier turns, that covers the title, town, gear, skills, couch HUD, attract, dev mode and each zone I could reach.\n\nWhat is still not done:\n- **60-minute pace:** the bot clears the campaign in 12 to 19 sim minutes, and nothing here can measure a human's pace.\n- **Screens not viewed:** Dame Brasse's and Mother Ogive's screens, the Stash, Writ board, Codex, Settings, Party, the touch-only message, and each class's casting animation. The touch page and the other full-screen layouts are covered only by the layout and browser tests.\n- **Malison's arms:** they are not driven by the engine's spring or arm-solver tools.\n- **Crawler's legs:** it swings as a bounded loop, not placed feet."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1241,"cache_read_input_tokens":929531,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1241},"output_tokens":770,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b7f78278-523d-4db5-bad6-0b641e53d240","uuid":"ff60d03e-0179-4dd9-99ab-2075ced92580","timestamp":"2026-11-06T05:17:43.327Z","request_id":"req_011Cgm7DoQ5EEDaKj7s5KQFt"}
