{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgm7RG2mAAecQJKCRnVos","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've now looked at almost every planned screen and fixed what looked wrong. The shell, layout and browser tests pass again on the rebuilt HTML (179 and 58 checks, 0 failures). I did not re-run the playthroughs, hub tier or sim tier after these last small UI edits; the sim code is untouched.\n\n**Fixed after viewing:**\n- Brasse's craft screen: the \"Reliquary\" and \"Legendary\" buttons were cut off, so they now read Relic and Legend.\n- Collection Box: the tab labels overlapped the BOX and YOUR PACK captions, so the tabs moved up.\n- Settings: the Back button overlapped the prompts, so the list is tighter.\n- Touch-only portrait screen: the attract tour's header ran off the screen and collided with the DEMO tag and the gear, and the \"controller or keyboard required\" message appeared twice. The header now wraps and the duplicate is gone. I did not re-view this one after the fix; the browser touch test passes.\n\n**Screens viewed (this turn and earlier):**\n- **Services and menus:** Dame Brasse, Mother Ogive, Pennywhistle, Collection Box, Writ board, Codex, Settings and Party.\n- **Hero and Knell screens:** gear, skills, Knell Font setup and About.\n- **World and shell:** title, town, couch HUD, attract, dev mode, map and dialogue.\n- **Zones and bosses:** every zone, the Bursar and Malison arenas, and the opening cutscene.\n- **Combat:** a Bellwarden fight shows hit numbers and the Clangor vessel filling.\n\n**Still open:**\n- **60-minute pace:** nothing here can measure a human's pace. The bot clears the campaign in 12 to 19 sim minutes.\n- **Malison's arms:** they sway through a hand-written animation, not the engine's spring or arm-solver tools.\n- **Crawler legs:** they swing on a fixed loop, not placed feet.\n- **Not viewed:** the Lamplighter and Sexton casting animations, and the Codex Bestiary, Lore and How to Play pages. The Codex Quests page was viewed; the Lamplighter and Sexton in play only appeared in other shots."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1262,"cache_read_input_tokens":948405,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1262},"output_tokens":750,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b7f78278-523d-4db5-bad6-0b641e53d240","uuid":"27f17b0c-d4e7-481a-86bf-476faa615f01","timestamp":"2026-11-06T05:20:19.996Z","request_id":"req_011Cgm7RFgftgwZASbfDjW9Q"}
