{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Bash, Monitor, Read</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n- The user ran `/goal`: \"Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says. Done when: Everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer is done, and everything TASK.md asks you to hand in is in this folder.\"\n- STAGE.md says: \"Build the game PLAN.md describes. Take your file names and what to hand in from TASK.md, which is filled in for you. Keep your progress in PROGRESS.md, so you can pick up where you were after your context is compacted.\"\n- TASK.md hand-ins (all present):\n  - A single HTML file named `[GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261105-162042].html` at the root, above the dev folder.\n  - A dev subfolder with the same name.\n  - `exit-interview.json` in the exact shape given.\n  - A final chat reply carrying Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback, plus the same four on the in-game About/Credits screen.\n- Key TASK.md and PLAN.md constraints:\n  - Build on the riftlight Pixel Engine, unedited.\n  - All audio synthesised in code; Animalese babble voices; music at 10% by default.\n  - Controller-first 10-foot UI with glyph switching (PlayStation default, Xbox option, keys and mouse).\n  - Touch-only devices show \"Controller or keyboard required\" and the settings button.\n  - Attract mode after 10 s idle.\n  - Dev mode with live sliders and Reset.\n  - AI Hub shared-world session (`github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub`).\n  - No TODOs or stubs.\n  - Tests are headless scripts behind one command; no subagents or workflows for review.\n  - Other agents share the machine. Only stop processes I started, by PID. Never use pkill, killall or fuser -k. Keep files inside my own folder. Use 127.0.0.1 and an OS-picked port for servers.\n  - Don't run `playwright install`.\n  - Run at most one or two browsers at once.\n- The Stop hook fired four times with the same message: \"Everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer\" is not done. Items it cited:\n  - 60-minute pace unchecked.\n  - Malison arms not driven by the engine's spring/arm-solver tools.\n  - Crawler legs a bounded loop, not placed feet.\n  - Cutscenes were overlays, not camera sequences.\n  - Not every screenshot viewed.\n  - Tiers not re-run after the last edits.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n- Pixel Engine 0.46.0 (three.js r186, Rapier, WebGPU, toon pixel renderer). Never edit `pixel-engine.js` or `session.js`; hashes are in `tools_hashes.txt`.\n- esbuild bundle into a single HTML via `tools/build.mjs`: session.js is the first script, the hub meta tags follow, then one module script. `tools/genabout.mjs` regenerates `about.generated.js` and `credits.generated.js` from `exit-interview.json` and `CREDITS.md`.\n- Sim/view split:\n  - `src/sim` is pure JS, deterministic, at 60 Hz, with no DOM and no Math.random.\n  - Events are drained by the view.\n  - NavGrid is built with `origin: [0,0,0]` so sim coordinates equal grid coordinates.\n  - Props are monsters with `prop:true`.\n  - `moveBy` collision radius is 0.3, with a wedge-escape rule.\n  - `walkable()` is cellAt-based; `nav.walkable` accepts out-of-bounds positions, so don't use it.\n  - Skills are data ops in `src/data/classes.js`, with 24 skills × 3 Tones and Vows.\n- Immediate-mode UI (`src/ui/ui.js`):\n  - Full-screen screens are laid out in a virtual 427×240 area, centred, via `ui.setVirtual` and a proxy hud.\n  - Focus moves on d-pad or stick; mouse hover moves focus.\n  - `setFocus(null)` is deferred to `endFrame`.\n  - Overlay toggle keys must ignore the frame the overlay was born (`overlay.born`).\n- Input router: keyboard, mouse and per-pad intents; the game is locked to `localSeat`; Options on an unowned pad joins couch co-op instead of pausing.\n- Hub netcode (`src/net/hubflow.js`):\n  - The host sim is authoritative; clients mirror snapshots (`s`) and events (`e`), and send intents (`i`) and commands (`c`).\n  - A game-owned card; `AIHub.finish` with standings and awards.\n  - `session.update` sets `game.sessionPaused = !playing()`.\n  - A server copy runs `Engine.headless`.\n- Testing:\n  - `tools/test.mjs [--sim|--headless|--browser|--hub]` prints only failures and a count.\n  - `tools/runtier.mjs` is a tiny runner.\n  - The bot playthrough is `tests/headless/playthrough.mjs`; run it with `PT_CLASS=0|1|2 PT_VERBOSE=1`, and `PT_DUMP=<minute>` dumps hero state.\n  - `tools/shot.mjs \"query\" frames out.png [w h]` with the `SHOT_JS` env takes screenshots.\n  - Long jobs are run in the background with output files, polled with `until grep -q \"^done\" file; do sleep; done` and `timeout`.\n- Balance knobs: `monsterXp` factor 0.7 (`src/sim/stats.js`); boss HP in `src/data/monsters.js` (Bursar 280, Ambrose 280, Malison 400, wardens 120/100/130). Malison has `hpFloor` phases in `bosses.js`: a floor of 0.62 until 55 s, 0.27 until 118 s, then 0.\n- Cut features (allowed by the plan, traces removed): Drowned Pantry, Sister Pyx, session level-up picks.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections (key ones):\n- `work/exit-interview.json`: final answers (39 issues, 19 critical); the animation line was updated to mention jointed legs and swaying rope arms. Valid JSON.\n- `work/PROGRESS.md`: progress log, updated through the final full-run entries.\n- Dev folder `tests/ISSUES.md`: 39 numbered issues (19 marked C).\n- `src/modes/game.js` (TollGame). Latest edits:\n  - `cine` boss-entrance cutscene: `onSimEvent` case 'bossStart' sets `this.cine = {t:2.6, dur:2.6, x, z}`; `tickTimers` sets `this.cut` and `cutZoom`; `fixedUpdate` returns while `cine.t > 0`; `drawMode` draws letterbox bars.\n  - `startNewGame` now does `enterZone('yard')` and then `playNarration()`.\n  - HUD is skipped during overlays 'narration', 'ending' and 'dialog'.\n- `src/ui/screens.js`:\n  - `drawNarration` rewritten as a camera cutscene: bars, drifting `game.cut` and `cutZoom`, subtitle in the lower bar, skip on ok.\n  - Map footer moved to `H-34`, with short zone names.\n  - Settings menu uses `y=28`, `h=13`.\n  - Death overlay, create flow and pause (closes only if `frame > overlay.born`).\n- `src/ui/screens_hero.js`: Stash tab labels moved up to y=20.\n- `src/ui/screens_town.js`: Brasse rarity buttons use the labels COMMON/BLESSED/RELIC/LEGEND.\n- `src/ui/screens_dev.js`: balance sliders show 9 rows (`const per = 9`).\n- `src/modes/attract.js`: header label wrapped, DEMO tag at left, duplicate touch message removed.\n- `src/view/models/bodies.js`: Tomb Crawler, Clapperjaw and Collection Plate legs are named pivot groups (`Leg0..`); Malison arms are pivot groups `Arm0..Arm3` (tubes).\n- `src/view/actors.js`:\n  - `swingLimbs(a, m, dt)` swings Leg and Arm pivots.\n  - Malison arms now use `SpringChain` (imported from the engine): segments 2, length 1.2, rest [0,-1,0], stiffness 3, keep 0.96, gravity 8. Root world position and basis come from `a.root.rotation.y`; tip offset is converted to `rotation.x/z`.\n- `src/sim/bosses.js`:\n  - Bosses are Bursar, Ambrose, Malison and wardens.\n  - Malison phases: phase 3 unhides ropes, and ropes marked `used` count toward death.\n  - `hpFloor` is set each tick, and `dealToMonster` in `core.js` clamps HP to `m.hpFloor`.\n  - Crumble pits restore after 9 s and emit a 'crumble' event with `restore`.\n  - On boss death, `bone_wall`, `hostile_ring` and `beams` areas are zeroed.\n  - The Chorister warden now flees only under 3.5 m.\n- `src/sim/bot.js`:\n  - Anti-stuck ignore memory.\n  - `mem.still`-based recentring.\n  - `goal.force` ignores targets beyond 1.2 m.\n  - Bosses are weighted 0.4 and nests 0.3 in target selection.\n  - Targets with `invuln > w.t+1` are ignored.\n  - `goal.pick` stops at 0.3 m.\n  - Casts skills only within reach.\n- `src/sim/campaign.js`:\n  - Quest 5 now has two steps (`climb`, `malison`).\n  - Authored boss arenas get an exit spot.\n  - The relic is placed at `exit.z-4.5`.\n- `src/sim/world.js`: `useSpot` marks ropes `used`; 'relic', 'box', 'gate', 'wagon' and 'novice' were added to the use cases.\n- `src/sim/core.js`:\n  - `spawnMonster` snaps to floor.\n  - Requiem bonus pays only at thresholds [10,25,50,100,200,400].\n  - `killMonster` handles props.\n- `src/sim/monsters.js`: `steer` uses a flow field aimed at the next cell centre; the boss tick call is `w.bossHooks.tick(w, m, tgt, DT)`; jammed monsters pass through each other (ghost).\n- `src/data/zones.js`: the knell zone now has `mon` and `elites` lists.\n- `tests/headless/playthrough.mjs`: bot driver with goals, services, inventory pruning, balance assertions (level 16–24, Bursar 60–180 s, Malison 120–300 s, ≥2 legendaries), a Knell Run at the end, and `PT_DUMP` debug output.\n- `tests/headless/{smoke,shell,layout,lastbell}.mjs`, `tests/browser/{boot,input,hub,hubgame}.mjs`, `tests/sim/{zones,combat,lint,systems}.mjs`.\n- `tools/test.mjs` tiers: sim; headless (smoke, shell, layout, lastbell, playthrough); browser (boot, input); hub (hub, hubgame).\n\n4. Errors and fixes (selected; all logged in `tests/ISSUES.md`):\n- NavGrid centred origin: fixed with `origin: [0,0,0]`.\n- Tutorial yard spawned trash and elites: skip when `def.gen.tutorial`.\n- Drops and scripted spawns inside walls: snapped to floor.\n- 'reach' quest steps advanced through a locked exit: `exitLock` check.\n- Relic use was a no-op: added to the use cases.\n- Coins crashed the loot view: handle 'coin'.\n- Foreclosure bone walls never lifted: cleared on boss death.\n- Authored arenas had no exit: added one.\n- Monsters deadlocked at doorways: ghost-through plus the steering fix.\n- Hero wedged in a doorway: wedge-escape in `moveBy`.\n- Class picker always chose the last card: deferred `setFocus(null)`.\n- Pause and Hero screens closed on their opening frame: `overlay.born` check.\n- Pad Options paused instead of joining: ownership check in router.\n- 49 layout overflows: virtual 427×240 layout.\n- Requiem XP compounding: thresholds.\n- Hub sessions never stepped the sim: `sessionPaused` deadlock fixed in `session.update`.\n- Boss timers used the distance variable `dt` instead of `DT`: fixed.\n- Crumble `nearestFloor` placed heroes outside the map: uses `walkable()`.\n- Ropes never counted `used`: fixed in `useSpot`.\n- Knell had no monsters: `ZONES.knell.mon` added.\n- Last Bell set pieces overwrote legendaries: picks avoid head and chest.\n- Bot oscillation and threshold chatter: `force` rule made unconditional.\n- Test-only fixes: the playthrough's rope progress (`+1.2` per tick) and the inventory-full softlock (sell commons and blessed).\n- Balance tuning: monsterXp 0.7, boss HP values, Malison `hpFloor`.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n- Solved: all tiers except headless passed on the last build (sim 1769, browser 58, hub 10).\n- Earlier green runs: each class playthrough (38 checks incl. Knell Run), lastbell 30 checks, shell 136+, layout 43.\n- Ongoing: the Sexton playthrough softlock in the summit step \"malison\" (see Current Work).\n\n6. All user messages:\n- `/goal`: \"Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says. Done when: Everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer is done, and everything TASK.md asks you to hand in is in this folder.\"\n- Stop hook feedback (×4), each saying the PLAN.md completion part is unmet:\n  - 1st: reduced models, cutscenes as overlays, the 60-minute pace unchecked, and \"I did not look at every screen\".\n  - 2nd: opening and ending cutscenes as overlays, Crawler, Clapperjaw and Plate not animated, Malison rope arms, pace unchecked, screens not reviewed.\n  - 3rd: the unviewed screens listed (Brasse/Ogive services, Stash, Writ board, Codex, Settings, Party, touch message, class casting), plus Malison arms, Crawler legs and pace.\n  - 4th: the same remaining items plus tiers not re-run after the last UI edits.\n- There were no other user messages beyond these and the system reminders. Most of the mid-run \"hasn't heard from you\" messages were system notices.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n- Fix the Sexton summit softlock so the headless tier passes. The hero stands still at about (12.4,4.5) while Malison's HP falls only ~12% in 285 s; phase 1 never advances, so ropes stay hidden.\n- Re-run the full test tiers (`node tools/test.mjs --sim/--browser/--hub/--headless`) and confirm all pass on a final build (`node tools/build.mjs`).\n- Open PLAN.md items still unmet:\n  - the 60-minute pace (not measurable here);\n  - the Crawler's placed feet (LegStepper) — its legs are a swing loop;\n  - Malison arms now use SpringChain, but the arm-solver (twoBoneIK) part is not done;\n  - screens not yet viewed: Codex Bestiary/Lore pages, a few others.\n- Final chat reply must stay accurate, with Source Information and the three feedback sections from `exit-interview.json`.\n\n8. Current Work:\n- Debugging the Sexton playthrough softlock in the summit with a temporary script `.dbg.mjs` in the dev folder (it should be deleted afterwards). The script:\n  - boots a quick start with cls 'sexton', zone 'summit', level 17, seed 4321;\n  - sets `w.camp.q = 4; w.camp.s = 1`;\n  - sets `h.bot = true`;\n  - sets `botGoal` to the visible unused rope (use, force) or the boss position;\n  - runs up to 60 steps of 300 frames, closing overlays and reviving, and prints boss HP%, phase, hero position and rope states.\n- Output showed the boss at 100% falling to 88% over 285 s, phase 1, ropes `hhh`, with the hero stationary at (12.4,4.5) from about 150 s.\n- Suspected causes:\n  - the bot stuck near the boss, or the Sexton's damage not landing on the hovering boss;\n  - the sim-freezing `cine` shifting timing and exposing the latent bot or design softlock.\n- Files were last modified before this: `src/view/actors.js` (SpringChain arms) and the new screenshots. The HTML was rebuilt after the SpringChain change and the full-tier run started.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n- Continue the debugging described above: find why the Sexton bot, or Malison, makes almost no progress in phase 1 (inspect the bot's target and cast state, and whether minions or skills hit the hovering boss).\n  - Fix options: have the bot move toward and attack the boss, or make Malison phase 1 damageable; the likely sim-side suspects are Malison's `hover`/`r:2.0` and `inArc`/`monstersNear` range.\n- Then delete `.dbg.mjs`, rebuild with `node tools/build.mjs`, and re-run the full headless tier (and the other tiers if sim code changed).\n- Most recent task text, verbatim: \"[Stop hook] Everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer is done, and everything TASK.md asks you to hand in is in this folder.\" The immediate last action was the debug run described above, with the Sexton \"malison\" step softlock at hero position 13.7,4.7.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/micha/.claude/projects/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-build-v2--20261105-162042--x14746a-work/b7f78278-523d-4db5-bad6-0b641e53d240.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b7f78278-523d-4db5-bad6-0b641e53d240","uuid":"c283bc1c-58bf-406d-8271-c008f3670c93","timestamp":"2026-1